{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Resampling Periodicity.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Resampling Periodicity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"resampling periodicity resampling periodicity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Resampling Periodicity.md","fileName":"Resampling Periodicity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Resampling Periodicity","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Copy-Move and Resampling Forensics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Copy-Move and Resampling Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Resampling Periodicity.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Resampling Periodicity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"resampling periodicity resampling periodicity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Resampling Periodicity.md","fileName":"Resampling Periodicity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Resampling Periodicity","heading":"Resampling Periodicity","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Resampling periodicity is the repeating pattern of prediction relationships created when an interpolation grid passes through an original pixel lattice. At some output positions the value depends strongly on a particular arrangement of neighbors, and that arrangement recurs at intervals determined by the scale or rotation.\n\nA detector estimates local linear dependencies and searches their strength for periodic structure. A localized response can expose a transformed insert, whereas an image-wide response may simply record benign resizing during publication.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Copy-Move and Resampling Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Resampling Periodicity.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Resampling Periodi